## What to deliver

Build and rig the spire up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a slim masonry spire base, a halo ring around
its crown, and a solar lens atop its tip. The required interface is the two auto
**`halo_ring_spin`** and **`lens_pulse`** joints that spin the ring a full
revolution and bob the lens up and down on their own, while the `base` stays
fixed, with the motion of both authored as F-curve animations. Produce **every**
required part, joint, and animation; you may add your own extra parts, joints, or
auto-play animations on top, but do not drop or contradict the required interface.
When you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your
finished submission.
